# MC-X-F9: two movements compared with ==. L §1 (P-4) and §5.14: "A movement, planned here or observed (§5.19), is a
# thing of its kind"; L §5.7: things "compare only by == and !=" (§5.6); a movement is one by its stable id (L §2.5).
# back[r] states item = r, so for r = get[2027-03] one refund has f.item == r (t), as comparing their days says (t2).
# snap11 refused t: LOAD-UNIT get[2027-01] and get[2027-03] compared.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind items: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
kind refunds: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
  attr item: key items
place acct: accounts PLN lives 2027-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2027-01-01..
move get[m in months]: items
  on start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to acct amount 0
move back[r in items over ..]: refunds
  on r.day
  attr item = r
  leg cash from acct to world amount 0
ask t: count(f in refunds over .. where f.item == r) for r in items over 2027-03
ask t2: count(f in refunds over .. where f.item.day == r.day) for r in items over 2027-03
=== expect
t (r = get[2027-03]): 1
  cut 2027-01-01
t2 (r = get[2027-03]): 1
  cut 2027-01-01
